    <!-- Article Header -->
    <header class="article-header">
        <h1>Your Ultimate Guide to Arlington's June 2026 Events: World Cup Fever Hits The American Dream City</h1>
        <p class="subtitle">From FIFA World Cup matches at AT&T Stadium to summer festivals and local happenings, discover everything happening in Arlington this June</p>
        <div class="article-meta">Published May 31, 2026 | Arlington Pulse</div>
    </header>
    
    <!-- Hero Image -->
    <div class="hero-image">
        <img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1577223625816-7546f13df25d?w=1200&h=675&fit=crop" alt="AT&T Stadium in Arlington Texas during a major event with crowds and excitement">
    </div>
    
    <!-- Article Content -->
    <article class="article-container">
        <div class="article-content">
            <p>June 2026 is shaping up to be one of the most exciting months in Arlington's history. As summer officially arrives in The American Dream City, something extraordinary is happening—Arlington is transforming into an international destination as <strong>AT&T Stadium hosts multiple FIFA World Cup 2026 matches</strong>, including the highly anticipated Netherlands vs. Japan showdown on June 14.</p>
            
            <p>But the World Cup is just the beginning. From wellness fairs to community celebrations, Arlington's June calendar is packed with events that showcase why this city continues to be one of the most vibrant destinations in Texas. Whether you're a local looking for weekend plans or a visitor experiencing Arlington for the first time, here's your complete guide to everything happening this month.</p>
            
            <h2>The Main Event: FIFA World Cup 2026 at AT&T Stadium</h2>
            
            <p>There's no bigger story this June than the FIFA World Cup coming to Arlington. <strong>AT&T Stadium will host 9 matches throughout the tournament</strong>, including a semi-final game that will bring soccer fans from around the globe to our city. The first match at the stadium kicks off on June 14 at 3 p.m. with Netherlands facing Japan—a clash that's already generating massive buzz among soccer enthusiasts.</p>
            
            <p>The tournament isn't just about the matches themselves. The entire Entertainment District will be buzzing with watch parties, fan zones, and international energy that Arlington has never experienced before. Local businesses are preparing for an influx of visitors, and the city is pulling out all the stops to ensure every guest experiences the best of what Arlington has to offer.</p>
            
            <p>If you're planning to attend, book your accommodations early and arrive with plenty of time to explore. The atmosphere around AT&T Stadium during World Cup matches is electric—think tailgating meets international festival, with food, music, and fans from every corner of the world coming together to celebrate the beautiful game.</p>
            
            <h2>Community Events: Wellness, Culture & Summer Fun</h2>
            
            <p>While the World Cup dominates headlines, Arlington Parks and Recreation has curated an incredible lineup of community events throughout June. Here are the highlights you won't want to miss:</p>
            
            <div class="event-card">
                <h3>Texas Health Arlington Memorial Wellness Fair</h3>
                <div class="event-date">June 5, 2026</div>
                <p>Kick off your summer wellness journey at this free community event bringing together health experts and local resources. From fitness demonstrations to nutrition workshops, this fair offers everything you need to live well, stay well, and thrive. It's the perfect way to start June with a focus on health and community connection.</p>
            </div>
            
            <div class="event-card">
                <h3>Juneteenth Celebration & Dallas Wings Game Trip</h3>
                <div class="event-date">June 17, 2026</div>
                <p>Experience a unique day trip that combines sports and cultural celebration. For just $40, you get lunch, transportation to College Park Center, and a ticket to watch the Dallas Wings basketball game while celebrating Juneteenth. It's an affordable way to enjoy professional sports and honor an important part of American history.</p>
            </div>
            
            <h2>Where to Eat, Drink & Celebrate</h2>
            
            <p>With all these events happening, you're going to need fuel. Fortunately, Arlington's food and drink scene is more exciting than ever. Here are five local businesses that should be on your radar this June:</p>
            
            <div class="business-listing">
                <h3><a href="https://www.thetipsyoak.com" target="_blank">The Tipsy Oak</a></h3>
                <p>This downtown favorite combines craft cocktails with an incredible patio atmosphere—perfect for pre-World Cup drinks or post-event celebrations. Their outdoor seating area is one of the best in the city, and the menu features locally-sourced ingredients that showcase Texas flavors.</p>
                <a href="https://www.thetipsyoak.com" class="business-link" target="_blank">Visit Website →</a>
            </div>
            
            <div class="business-listing">
                <h3><a href="https://divisionbrewing.com" target="_blank">Division Brewing</a></h3>
                <p>Located in the heart of the Urban Union District, Division Brewing has become a cornerstone of Arlington's craft beer scene. With rotating taps featuring experimental brews and classic styles, it's the ideal spot to grab a cold one after a day of World Cup excitement or community events.</p>
                <a href="https://divisionbrewing.com" class="business-link" target="_blank">Visit Website →</a>
            </div>
            
            <div class="business-listing">
                <h3><a href="https://hurtadobbq.com" target="_blank">Hurtado Barbecue</a></h3>
                <p>When it comes to Texas barbecue, Hurtado is in a league of its own. Their brisket has earned regional acclaim, and the downtown location puts you right in the middle of the action. Whether you're feeding a group of soccer fans or just craving authentic Texas smoke, this is your spot.</p>
                <a href="https://hurtadobbq.com" class="business-link" target="_blank">Visit Website →</a>
            </div>
            
            <div class="business-listing">
                <h3><a href="https://www.texas-live.com" target="_blank">Texas Live!</a></h3>
                <p>The entertainment epicenter of Arlington, Texas Live! is gearing up for massive World Cup watch parties and summer events. With multiple venues under one roof, restaurants, bars, and outdoor spaces, it's the ultimate destination for groups looking to soak up the June energy.</p>
                <a href="https://www.texas-live.com" class="business-link" target="_blank">Visit Website →</a>
            </div>
            
            <div class="business-listing">
                <h3><a href="https://salterbroscoffee.com" target="_blank">Salter Bros. Coffee Roasters</a></h3>
                <p>For those early morning World Cup matches or a midday caffeine fix between events, Salter Bros. delivers some of the best coffee in DFW. Their downtown location has become a community gathering spot where locals and visitors alike connect over expertly roasted beans.</p>
                <a href="https://salterbroscoffee.com" class="business-link" target="_blank">Visit Website →</a>
            </div>
            
            <h2>Planning Your June Visit</h2>
            
            <p>If you're visiting Arlington for the World Cup or any of June's events, here are a few tips to make the most of your experience:</p>
            
            <p><strong>Book Early:</strong> Hotels fill up fast during major events. The Entertainment District offers the most convenient access to AT&T Stadium, but downtown Arlington provides a more local experience with easy access to unique restaurants and shops.</p>
            
            <p><strong>Use Public Transit:</strong> With increased traffic expected, consider using Arlington's Via rideshare service or hotel shuttles to get around. Parking near AT&T Stadium can be challenging on event days.</p>
            
            <p><strong>Explore Beyond the Stadium:</strong> While the World Cup is the main attraction, don't miss the chance to explore River Legacy Parks, the Arlington Museum of Art, or the vibrant downtown scene. Arlington has so much more to offer than just sports.</p>
            
            <h2>Why June 2026 Matters for Arlington</h2>
            
            <p>This isn't just another summer month for Arlington—it's a coming-out party on the world stage. The FIFA World Cup represents the largest international event the city has ever hosted, and the economic and cultural impact will be felt for years to come.</p>
            
            <p>But beyond the global spotlight, June 2026 showcases what makes Arlington special year-round: a community that knows how to come together, local businesses that pour their hearts into everything they do, and a city that's constantly evolving while staying true to its roots.</p>
            
            <p>Whether you're cheering for your favorite soccer team at AT&T Stadium, discovering a new favorite restaurant downtown, or simply enjoying a Texas summer evening on a patio with friends, June in Arlington is an experience you won't forget.</p>
            
            <p>Get out there and make some memories. The American Dream City is waiting.</p>
            
